# ==============================================================================
# Example 50: Multi-Species Ecosystem — E. coli + Synechocystis
# ==============================================================================
#
# This example demonstrates the build_multi_species_ecosystem() API
# (doc/22 §18, Phase I) by simulating a mixed heterotroph + phototroph
# ecosystem in a shared chemostat environment.
#
# Species:
#   1. E. coli K-12 MG1655 — heterotroph consuming glucose
#   2. Synechocystis PCC 6803 — photoautotroph fixing CO₂
#
# The ecosystem uses GEM-driven growth (gem_driven=True) so each species'
# growth rate is determined by FBA solved from its metabolic model.
#
# Cross-feeding: E. coli produces CO₂ (from respiration) which Synechocystis
# can fix via the Calvin cycle. Synechocystis produces O₂ (from photosystem II)
# which E. coli requires for aerobic respiration.
#
# Expected behavior:
#   - Both species grow from their initial biomass
#   - Glucose is consumed by E. coli
#   - CO₂ is consumed by Synechocystis
#   - O₂ is produced by Synechocystis, consumed by E. coli
#   - Ecosystem reaches a steady state or coexistence
# ==============================================================================

#species name=ecoli genome=ecoli_k12 substrate=glucose vmax=0.02 ks=0.1
#species name=synecho genome=synechocystis substrate=co2 photo=true photo_vmax=0.01

#patch name=env kind=chemostat width=5 height=5 flow_rate=0.001
#  initial.biomass ecoli=10.0 synecho=5.0
#  substrate glucose initial=10.0 bulk=10.0 carbon_per_mol=6
#  substrate co2 initial=5.0 bulk=5.0 carbon_per_mol=1
#  substrate oxygen initial=0.25 bulk=0.25 carbon_per_mol=0
#end

#config backend=ecosystem ticks=500 gem_driven=true

#sim output=tick,biomass_ecoli,biomass_synecho,glucose,co2,oxygen
